      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome in. What brings you to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S003",
      "patient_response": "Well, I guess what brings me in is... it's been happening a lot at the museum. I help out there a bit since I stopped working. We have this big art walk coming up. Actually, the art walk used to be on Thursdays, but they moved it to Saturdays because the downtown businesses complained about the parking. Parking is just a total nightmare down there now since the city put in those new bike lanes. I don't even own a bicycle anymore, my knees just can't take the pedaling, especially on those hills. \n\nBut anyway, what happens is, people at the museum will be talking right to me about the next art walk, and I’ll be looking right at them, but then I suddenly realize I completely missed the middle of what they said. I end up having to ask them to run it by me again. It's just getting a bit embarrassing.",
