    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Growing up or even now, have you ever had trouble sitting still or felt an inner sense of restlessness?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, not really. I've never been much of a fidgeter. I can actually sit still for hours, especially if I'm in my favorite recliner. It's this old La-Z-Boy I bought back in, oh, must have been '98, from a Sears that was going out of business at the mall. You know, it's a real shame what happened to Sears. You used to be able to buy absolutely anything from their catalog. I mean, people used to buy whole houses from them! My great-uncle actually lived in a Sears kit house up in Michigan. Had the original hardwood floors and everything. It was a beautiful place, right near a lake where we'd go fishing for bluegill every summer. I haven't been fishing in years, though... the mosquitoes just eat me alive. \n\nBut anyway, what were we talking about? Oh, right, sitting still. Yeah, no, I've never really had that restless feeling. I can just sit and watch the birds out the window all afternoon without feeling the need to jump up or move around.",
